SDK and operator subprocesses use owned Linux process groups. The driver waits
for its direct children, kills group descendants, then retains ownership until
two bounded Linux `/proc` snapshots establish every group member terminal or
absent. Unknown/unreadable/nonterminal verification retains the owned group and
the result is FAIL. A terminal orphan zombie may remain under PID1; Node does not
waitpid that non-child. It finalizes all41 cases after crashes, SIGKILLs and hangs
of the SDK child. Qualification, deployment/codegen and cleanup final/error
receipts use exclusively their initially guarded output binding, never a second
private/target/key preflight after shutdown. Canonical/no-alias/exclusive output
checks still apply. No OS sandbox is claimed.

